= 2k + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ContentVarianceLeadingConstant.vA_summand_partial_fractions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ContentVarianceLeadingConstant.vA_summand_partial_fractions","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/ContentVarianceLeadingConstant.lean#L29-L47","doc":"**Partial-fraction decomposition of the `v_A` summand (sorry-free).**\n\nFor `x ≠ 0, 2, −2` in any field,\n\n    1/(x(x²−4)²) = 1/(16x) − 1/(32(x−2)) − 1/(32(x+2)) + 1/(32(x−2)²) − 1/(32(x+2)²).\n\nThis is the elementary identity underlying `Σ_{n odd} 1/[n(n²−4)²] = 1/8`: summed over odd `n`, the\n`1/(16x)`, `1/(x∓2)` linear parts telescope (the divergent tail cancels, coefficient\n`1/16 − 1/32 − 1/32 = 0`) and the `1/(x∓2)²` quadratic parts telescope (the `π²/8` tail cancels),\nleaving the rational value `1/8`. Here only the per-term algebra is asserted. ","signatureChunk":0}]}